00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.760
And what you can see hopefully, is that

165
00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:42.880
by clicking play on the backlog, we've spun up three separate computers.

166
00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:46.400
For those three agents that are working on those three different tasks.

167
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.520
One of them is adding a dark mode toggle.

168
00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.200
Another one of them is fixing a bug.

169
00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:55.080
Another one is adding like customized categories.

170
00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:59.000
And so what you can see here is that we've gone

171
00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.840
we ended up down this sort of rabbit

172
00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:05.400
hole of like, okay, if you've got

173
00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:10.760
if you want like a good background agent experience

174
00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.520
that feels like a foreground agent experience,

175
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.880
you end up implementing GPU accelerated desktops

176
00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.280
because non GPU accelerated desktops are not very nice to use.

177
00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:25.680
But if we're doing AI infrastructure, we've got some GPUs lying around.

178
00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.360
And it just so happens that the same GPUs are used for inference.

179
00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.680
A lot of them also support

180
00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.080
like what GPUs were originally for which is graphics,

181
00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:34.800
and they also support hardware video encoding.

182
00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.840
So we borrowed a lot of the technology from the gaming industry.

183
00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:40.840
I don't know if anyone's ever played like

184
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.520
computer games in the cloud.

185
00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.480
It's actually possible to get pretty low latency and good performance.

186
00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.920
So so we're using the same the same tech as that.

